<script data-page="app" type="application/json">{"component":"flashcards\/study","props":{"errors":{},"name":"Topwords","auth":{"user":{"id":5,"name":"\u00c1rp\u00e1d Szaniszl\u00f3","email":"developedbybarley@gmail.com","email_verified_at":null,"two_factor_confirmed_at":null,"streak":1,"quiz_completions":0,"text_analyses":12,"last_activity_date":"2026-05-01T00:00:00.000000Z","onboarding_completed_at":"2026-04-18T19:40:25.000000Z","created_at":"2026-04-18T19:40:03.000000Z","updated_at":"2026-05-01T16:24:52.000000Z","stripe_id":"cus_UR8u0ziMkWwJIo","pm_type":null,"pm_last_four":null,"trial_ends_at":null,"ai_access":false,"subscriptions":[]},"isAdmin":true,"subscription":{"hasActiveAccess":true,"isSubscribed":false,"isPremium":false,"hasAiAccess":false,"isOnTrial":false}},"sidebarOpen":true,"flash":{"streakTriggered":null,"success":null,"achievements":[],"calibrationPrompt":null,"showTour":false,"importedCardId":null},"deck":{"id":10,"name":"Prev"},"cards":[{"id":51226,"front":"<p>I think I _______ my ankle playing soccer yesterday. <em>(megr\u00e1ndul \/ kibicsakl\u00f3dik)<\/em><\/p><p>The doctor advised him to rest and avoid putting weight on the _______ joint. <em>(megs\u00e9r\u00fclt \/ kificamodott)<\/em><\/p><p>Ligamentous _______ is a common sports injury, often resulting from sudden twisting or inversion of the foot. <em>(r\u00e1ndul\u00e1s \/ ficam)<\/em><\/p><p>She winced as she tried to stand, the sharp pain a clear indication that she had _______ her wrist. <em>(megr\u00e1nd\u00edtott \/ kificam\u00edtott)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">megr\u00e1ndul \/ kificamodik \/ ficamosodik \/ elcsavarodik<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): meggy\u00f3gyul \/ meger\u0151s\u00f6dik \/ felfriss\u00fcl<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ your ankle = megr\u00e1nd\u00edtani a bok\u00e1t (pl. He _______ his ankle badly.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ your wrist = megr\u00e1nd\u00edtani a csukl\u00f3t (pl. She fell and _______ her wrist.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 ligament _______ = \u00edz\u00fcleti szalag s\u00e9r\u00fcl\u00e9s (pl. The most common type of _______ is a ligament _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ injury = r\u00e1ndul\u00e1sos s\u00e9r\u00fcl\u00e9s (pl. He has a mild _______ injury.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>sprain<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>sprain<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>sprain<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: sprained ankle \/ sprained wrist \/ sprained ligament \/ sprain injury<\/span><\/p><p>similar: twist \/ wrench \/ strain \/ dislocate<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: heal \/ recover \/ strengthen<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"15 perc","good":"30 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-01T23:01:43+00:00"},{"id":49593,"front":"<p>He felt guilty about his _______ thoughts during the sermon. <em>(b\u0171n\u00f6s \/ erk\u00f6lcstelen)<\/em><\/p><p>The novel explored the _______ desires that led to the protagonist&#039;s downfall. <em>(b\u0171n\u00f6s \/ erk\u00f6lcstelen \/ romlott)<\/em><\/p><p>Many religious traditions condemn _______ acts as a violation of divine law. <em>(b\u0171n\u00f6s \/ istentelen \/ erk\u00f6lcstelen)<\/em><\/p><p>The detective suspected a _______ motive behind the seemingly random crime. <em>(rosszindulat\u00fa \/ gonosz \/ b\u0171n\u00f6s)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">b\u0171n\u00f6s \/ erk\u00f6lcstelen \/ gonosz \/ istentelen \/ rosszindulat\u00fa<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): er\u00e9nyes \/ j\u00e1mbor \/ szent<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ thoughts = b\u0171n\u00f6s gondolatok (pl. He tried to push away his _______ thoughts.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ desires = b\u0171n\u00f6s v\u00e1gyak (pl. The character was consumed by _______ desires.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ acts = b\u0171n\u00f6s cselekedetek (pl. The court found him guilty of several _______ acts.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ motive = b\u0171n\u00f6s ind\u00edt\u00e9k (pl. The police are investigating a _______ motive.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>sinful<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>sinful<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>sinfully<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>sinfulness<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: sinful thoughts \/ sinful desires \/ sinful acts \/ sinful nature<\/span><\/p><p>similar: wicked \/ immoral \/ unholy \/ corrupt<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: virtuous \/ righteous \/ holy<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":3,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"4 nap","good":"4 nap","easy":"5 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-01T20:46:15+00:00"},{"id":19316,"front":"<p>Drivers must navigate the _______ carefully to avoid collisions. <em>(k\u00f6rforgalom \/ karik\u00e1s \u00fat)<\/em><\/p><p>The town council decided to install a _______ at the busy intersection. <em>(k\u00f6rforgalom \/ forgalomir\u00e1ny\u00edt\u00f3 sziget)<\/em><\/p><p>Follow the signs and take the third exit from the _______. <em>(k\u00f6rforgalom \/ k\u00f6r alak\u00fa \u00fat)<\/em><\/p><p>He was unfamiliar with the local traffic laws and missed his turn at the _______. <em>(k\u00f6rforgalom \/ csom\u00f3pont)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">k\u00f6rforgalom \/ forgalomir\u00e1ny\u00edt\u00f3 sziget \/ k\u00f6r alak\u00fa \u00fat \/ csom\u00f3pont \/ keresztez\u0151d\u00e9s<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): egyenes \u00fat \/ k\u00f6zvetlen \u00fat \/ egyszer\u0171 keresztez\u0151d\u00e9s<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 enter the _______ = bel\u00e9pni a k\u00f6rforgalomba (pl. You need to signal before you enter the roundabout.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 exit the _______ = elhagyni a k\u00f6rforgalmat (pl. Take the second exit from the roundabout.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 drive around the _______ = k\u00f6r\u00f6zni a k\u00f6rforgalomban (pl. He got confused and ended up driving around the roundabout twice.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 navigate the _______ = navig\u00e1lni a k\u00f6rforgalomban (pl. It&#039;s important to navigate the roundabout safely.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p>noun: <strong>roundabout<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: traffic roundabout \/ mini roundabout \/ large roundabout \/ enter the roundabout<\/span><\/p><p>similar: traffic circle \/ rotary \/ traffic island \/ circular intersection<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: straight road \/ direct route \/ intersection<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":3,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"4 nap","good":"4 nap","easy":"5 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-04T19:07:18+00:00"},{"id":49598,"front":"<p>After standing up too quickly, I felt a bit _______ and had to sit back down. <em>(sz\u00e9d\u00fcl \/ megingott)<\/em><\/p><p>The patient reported experiencing episodes of _______, particularly when changing positions. <em>(sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u00e9s \/ egyens\u00falyveszt\u00e9s)<\/em><\/p><p>The rapid ascent in the hot air balloon induced a sense of _______ in some passengers. <em>(sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u00e9s \/ lebeg\u00e9s \u00e9rz\u00e9se)<\/em><\/p><p>The swirling patterns on the canvas created a _______ effect, making it hard to focus. <em>(sz\u00e9d\u00edt\u0151 \/ megd\u00f6bbent\u0151)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u0151 \/ sz\u00e9d\u00fclt \/ b\u00f3dult \/ lebeg\u0151 \/ megingott<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): stabil \/ kiegyens\u00falyozott \/ biztos<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 feeling _______ = sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u0151nek \u00e9rzi mag\u00e1t (pl. I&#039;m feeling a bit _______ today.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ in the head = fejben sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u00e9s (pl. He complained of _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ from heights = magass\u00e1gt\u00f3l val\u00f3 sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u00e9s (pl. She suffers from _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ sensation = sz\u00e9d\u00edt\u0151 \u00e9rz\u00e9s (pl. The roller coaster ride gave me a _______.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>dizzy<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>dizzy<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>dizziness<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: feeling dizzy \/ dizzy spells \/ dizzy from heights \/ dizzy head<\/span><\/p><p>similar: light-headed \/ vertiginous \/ woozy \/ giddy<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: steady \/ balanced \/ firm<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":3,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"4 nap","good":"4 nap","easy":"5 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-01T20:31:10+00:00"},{"id":49573,"front":"<p>The faster car managed to _______ the slower one on the highway. <em>(el\u0151z \/ lek\u00f6r\u00f6z)<\/em><\/p><p>She was determined to _______ her competitors in the race. <em>(fel\u00fclm\u00fal \/ legy\u0151z)<\/em><\/p><p>The company hopes to _______ its rivals in market share next year. <em>(megel\u0151z \/ fel\u00fclm\u00fal)<\/em><\/p><p>The new technology is expected to _______ the old methods. <em>(elavultt\u00e1 tesz \/ fel\u00fclm\u00fal)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">el\u0151z \/ lek\u00f6r\u00f6z \/ megel\u0151z \/ fel\u00fclm\u00fal \/ utol\u00e9r<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): lemarad \/ h\u00e1tr\u00e1ltat \/ lass\u00edt<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a car = aut\u00f3t megel\u0151zni (pl. He tried to overtake a car.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ the competition = lek\u00f6r\u00f6zni a versenyt\u00e1rsakat (pl. Our goal is to overtake the competition.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a lead = el\u0151nyt szerezni (pl. The team managed to overtake a significant lead.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ someone in a race = valakit megel\u0151zni egy versenyben (pl. She was able to overtake him in the final lap.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p>noun: <strong>overtaking<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>overtake<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: overtake a car \/ overtake the competition \/ overtake a lead \/ overtake in a race<\/span><\/p><p>similar: surpass \/ outstrip \/ outdo \/ get ahead of<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: fall behind \/ lag \/ be overtaken<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":1,"lapses":1,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"15 perc","good":"30 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-02T16:31:04+00:00"},{"id":49598,"front":"<p>After standing up too quickly, I felt a bit _______ and had to sit back down. <em>(sz\u00e9d\u00fcl \/ megingott)<\/em><\/p><p>The patient reported experiencing episodes of _______, particularly when changing positions. <em>(sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u00e9s \/ egyens\u00falyveszt\u00e9s)<\/em><\/p><p>The rapid ascent in the hot air balloon induced a sense of _______ in some passengers. <em>(sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u00e9s \/ lebeg\u00e9s \u00e9rz\u00e9se)<\/em><\/p><p>The swirling patterns on the canvas created a _______ effect, making it hard to focus. <em>(sz\u00e9d\u00edt\u0151 \/ megd\u00f6bbent\u0151)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u0151 \/ sz\u00e9d\u00fclt \/ b\u00f3dult \/ lebeg\u0151 \/ megingott<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): stabil \/ kiegyens\u00falyozott \/ biztos<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 feeling _______ = sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u0151nek \u00e9rzi mag\u00e1t (pl. I&#039;m feeling a bit _______ today.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ in the head = fejben sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u00e9s (pl. He complained of _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ from heights = magass\u00e1gt\u00f3l val\u00f3 sz\u00e9d\u00fcl\u00e9s (pl. She suffers from _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ sensation = sz\u00e9d\u00edt\u0151 \u00e9rz\u00e9s (pl. The roller coaster ride gave me a _______.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>dizzy<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>dizzy<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>dizziness<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: feeling dizzy \/ dizzy spells \/ dizzy from heights \/ dizzy head<\/span><\/p><p>similar: light-headed \/ vertiginous \/ woozy \/ giddy<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: steady \/ balanced \/ firm<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":3,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"4 nap","good":"4 nap","easy":"5 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-01T20:24:20+00:00"},{"id":49597,"front":"<p>She held the delicate flower gently in the _______ of her hand. <em>(teny\u00e9r \/ k\u00e9z bels\u0151 r\u00e9sze)<\/em><\/p><p>The company&#039;s success was attributed to its strategic _______ of market trends. <em>(felhaszn\u00e1l\u00e1s \/ kihaszn\u00e1l\u00e1s \/ alkalmaz\u00e1s)<\/em><\/p><p>The ancient text described a ritual involving the tracing of celestial patterns on the _______. <em>(teny\u00e9r \/ f\u00f6ldfelsz\u00edn \/ fel\u00fclet)<\/em><\/p><p>He felt a slight tremor in his _______ as he waited for the results. <em>(teny\u00e9r \/ k\u00e9z)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">teny\u00e9r \/ teny\u00e9rb\u00e9li \/ teny\u00e9rnyi \/ teny\u00e9rbe \/ teny\u00e9rb\u0151l<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): k\u00f6r\u00f6m \/ csukl\u00f3 \/ k\u00e9zfej<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 in the _______ of your hand = a kezed tenyer\u00e9ben (pl. The coin felt warm in the _______ of his hand.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ reading = teny\u00e9rj\u00f3sl\u00e1s (pl. She was interested in _______ reading.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ of a leaf = lev\u00e9l tenyere\/lapja (pl. The intricate veins spread across the _______ of the leaf.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ of a glove = keszty\u0171 tenyere (pl. The leather on the _______ of the glove was worn smooth.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>palm<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>palmate<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>palm<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>palm<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: hand palm \/ palm tree \/ palm reading \/ palm oil<\/span><\/p><p>similar: hand \/ palm tree \/ leaf \/ surface<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: back of the hand \/ fingertips \/ knuckles<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":3,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"4 nap","good":"4 nap","easy":"5 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-02T16:31:51+00:00"},{"id":51249,"front":"<p>There was a _______ hint of garlic in the sauce that made it delicious. <em>(finom \/ enyhe)<\/em><\/p><p>The politician&#039;s speech contained a _______ criticism of the opposing party&#039;s policies. <em>(burkolt \/ nem egy\u00e9rtelm\u0171)<\/em><\/p><p>The research identified a _______ correlation between the two variables, requiring further investigation. <em>(apr\u00f3 \/ nem nyilv\u00e1nval\u00f3)<\/em><\/p><p>She wore a dress with a _______ pattern of tiny flowers, almost imperceptible at first glance. <em>(apr\u00f3 \/ diszkr\u00e9t)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">finom \/ enyhe \/ burkolt \/ apr\u00f3 \/ diszkr\u00e9t<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): nyilv\u00e1nval\u00f3 \/ felt\u0171n\u0151 \/ er\u0151s<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ difference = finom k\u00fcl\u00f6nbs\u00e9g (pl. There&#039;s a subtle difference between these two shades of blue.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ hint = finom utal\u00e1s (pl. He gave a subtle hint that he wanted to leave.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ change = enyhe v\u00e1ltoz\u00e1s (pl. We noticed a subtle change in his behavior.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ criticism = burkolt kritika (pl. Her review contained subtle criticism of the author&#039;s style.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>subtle<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>subtle<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>subtly<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>subtlety<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: subtle difference \/ subtle hint \/ subtle change \/ subtle way<\/span><\/p><p>similar: delicate \/ fine \/ nuanced \/ understated<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: obvious \/ apparent \/ bla